'''''Taraxacum estrelense''''' is an [[apomixis|apomictic]] species of [[Taraxacum|dandelion]],<ref name="newsp">{{cite journal |last1=Galán de Mera |first1=A. |last2=Vicente Orellana |first2=J. A. |title=A new species of ''Taraxacum'' sect. ''Celtica'' (Asteraceae) from the Portuguese mountains |journal=Nordic Journal of Botany |date=2008 |volume=26 |pages=361–363 |doi=10.1111/j.1756-1051.2008.00275.x}}</ref> known from the [[Serra da Estrela]] and [[Peneda-Gerês National Park|Gerês]] mountain ranges in [[Portugal]], and the [[Galician Massif|Courel]] range in [[Spain]].<ref name="iberica">{{cite book |last1=Galán de Mera |first1=A. |title=Flora Iberica: Plantas vasculares de la Península Ibérica e Islas Baleares. Vol. XVI(II). Compositae (partim)|editor-last1= Talavera |editor-first1=S.|editor-last2= Buira|editor-first2=A.|editor-last3= Quintanar|editor-first3=A.|editor-last4= García|editor-first4=M.Á.|editor-last5= Talavera|editor-first5=M.|editor-last6= Fernández Piedra|editor-first6= P.|editor-last7= Aedo|editor-first7= C.|chapter=49. ''Taraxacum'' F.H. Wigg. [nom. cons.]|date=2017 |publisher=Real Jardín Botánico, CSIC |location=Madrid |pages=963–1062 |url=https://bibdigital.rjb.csic.es/viewer/16361/?offset=#page=255&viewer=picture&o=bookmark&n=0&q=triforme |access-date=16 September 2023}}</ref> It belongs to [[Section (botany)|sect.]] ''Celtica''.<ref name="newsp" />

== Description ==
''Taraxacum estrelense'' is a medium-sized dandelion up to 30&nbsp;cm tall, larger than the related ''[[Taraxacum triforme]]'' and ''[[Taraxacum algarbiense]]'' from southern Portugal. It has purple-spotted leaves with highly recurved and toothed leaf lobes. Pollen is scarce and produced only by the external flowers of the [[Pseudanthium|capitulum]]. The external [[Phyllary|phyllaries]] of the capitula have an inconspicuous white border. Achenes are olive-green, occasionally pink-streaked, with a discoloured [[Pappus (botany)|pappus]].<ref name="newsp" /><ref name="iberica" />

Records of ''Taraxacum algarbiense'' from Serra da Estrela refer to this species.<ref name="newsp" />

